&reftitle.description;
private Time\Duration::__construct
This private constructor prevents Time\Duration objects from being created with new. Use one of the factory methods instead, which make the unit of the given value explicit: Time\Duration::fromSeconds, Time\Duration::fromNanoseconds, Time\Duration::fromMicroseconds, Time\Duration::fromMilliseconds, Time\Duration::fromMinutes, Time\Duration::fromHours, or Time\Duration::fromIso8601DurationString.

&reftitle.errors;

 Attempting to instantiate the class with new throws an
 Error.

  &reftitle.examples;

   Creating a Time\Duration


<?php
try {
    $duration = new Time\Duration();
} catch (Error $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), PHP_EOL;
}

$duration = Time\Duration::fromSeconds(5);
var_dump($duration);


